# Adsorptive removal of diclofenac sodium from water with Zr-based metal–organic frameworks

Zubair Hasan 1, Nazmul Abedin Khan, Sung Hwa Jhung

Department of Chemistry and Green-Nano Materials Research Center, Kyungpook National University, Daegu 702-701, Republic of Korea

# h i g h l i g h t s

- Diclofenac sodium can be adsorbed effectively over UiO-66-SO\(_3\)H. The adsorption capacity and rate over UiO-66-SO\(_3\)H are remarkably high. The UiO-66-SO\(_3\)H can be used especially at low concentration of diclofenac sodium. The adsorption might be explained with electrostatic and acid–base interactions.

